## 9. Smart Contract Design & Security

This section details the on–chain contract architecture for the Blockchain Core component, including module breakdown, interfaces, upgradeability, security analyses, and gas‐optimization.

### 9.1 Module Breakdown

1. **SmartChequeFactory**
    - Responsibilities
    • Deploy new `SmartChequeEscrow` instances
    • Record registry of all deployed cheque addresses
    • Emit `ChequeCreated` events
    - Key Functions
    • `createSmartCheque(buyer, seller, token, totalAmount, milestones, expiration, metadata) → chequeAddress`
    • `getAllCheques() → address[]`
    - Events
    • `event ChequeCreated(address indexed cheque, address indexed buyer, address indexed seller)`
2. **SmartChequeEscrow**
    - Responsibilities
    • Lock stablecoins in escrow
    • Track milestone states (`Pending`, `Completed`, `Disputed`, `Released`)
    • Release funds upon milestone verification
    • Handle dispute flags and refunds
    - Key Functions
    • `lockFunds()` (caller = buyer)
    • `releaseFunds(uint256 milestoneId, bytes oracleProof)`
    • `openDispute(string reason)`
    • `resolveDispute(bool releaseFundsToSeller)`
    - Events
    • `FundsLocked(address indexed buyer, uint256 amount)`
    • `FundsReleased(uint256 indexed milestoneId, uint256 amount)`
    • `DisputeOpened(address indexed initiator, string reason)`
    • `DisputeResolved(address resolver, bool released)`
3. **ObligationRegistry**
    - Responsibilities
    • Store obligation hashes and pointers to oracle feeds
    • Allow lookup of obligations by cheque and milestone
    - Key Functions
    • `registerObligation(address cheque, uint256 milestoneId, bytes32 obligationHash, address oracleFeed)`
    • `getObligation(address cheque, uint256 milestoneId) → (bytes32, address)`
4. **DisputeManager**
    - Responsibilities
    • Centralize multi‐tier dispute logic across all cheques
    • Enforce escalation paths (AI, stakeholder, human arbitrator)
    • Record dispute lifecycle
    - Key Functions
    • `escalateDispute(address cheque, uint256 disputeId)`
    • `applyResolution(address cheque, uint256 disputeId, bool releaseToSeller)`
    - Events
    • `DisputeEscalated(address indexed cheque, uint256 indexed disputeId)`
    • `DisputeResolved(address indexed cheque, uint256 indexed disputeId, bool released)`

