# 11. Networking & Security Architecture

Below is the Blockchain Core’s network and security design, aligned with leading security best practices in 2025 (zero-trust, micro-segmentation, continuous compliance).

---

## 11.1 Zero-Trust VPC & Subnet Segmentation

- **Zero-Trust Model**
    
    • Implicit “deny all” by default; explicit allow only.
    
    • Mutual TLS (mTLS) between all services (API ↔ nodes ↔ indexer).
    
- **VPC Structure**
    - Single environment VPC (`10.0.0.0/16`), subdivided by function and trust level:
        1. **Ingress Zone** – Public ALB, Bastion, NAT Gateways
        2. **Application Zone** – API Gateway, Sequencers, Indexers
        3. **Data Zone** – Full & Archive Nodes, Databases, Vault
        4. **Management Zone** – CI/CD runners, Monitoring, HSM appliances
- **Subnet Isolation**
    
    
    | Zone | Subnet Type | CIDR | Egress |
    | --- | --- | --- | --- |
    | Ingress | Public | /24 per AZ | ALB → Internet |
    | Application | Private–App | /24 per AZ | mTLS only to peers |
    | Data | Private–Data | /26 per AZ | mTLS to App, Vault |
    | Management | Isolated | /28 per AZ | None; VPN only |
- **Routing**
    
    • No Internet egress from Data & Management zones
    
    • Private subnets use dedicated NAT in Ingress zone
    

---

## 11.2 Micro-Segmentation & Firewall Policies

- **Security Groups (SG)**
    - Fine-grained rules: one SG per role
    - Explicit mTLS port allowances (TCP 443 mutual auth)
- **Network ACLs**
    - Stateless filtering to block known bad IP ranges (threat intelligence feeds)
    - Geo-fencing: restrict inbound to approved geographies
- **Host-Level Protection**
    - eBPF-based firewalls (Cilium) for process-level controls
    - Runtime Application Self-Protection (RASP) agents in all containers

---

## 11.3 API Gateway & WAF

- **API Gateway**
    - AWS ALB or GCP HTTPS LB with mTLS front-to-back
    - JWT authentication at edge via Lambda@Edge or Cloud Run auth filter
- **Web Application Firewall**
    - OWASP CRS v4+, tuned with AI-driven anomaly detection
    - Custom rules for blockchain RPC patterns (e.g. block header fuzzing)
    - Bot management: CAPTCHA challenges for unusual traffic
- **DDoS Mitigation**
    - Native Shield Advanced / Cloud Armor with real-time traffic anomaly alerts
    - Elastic load-shedding at edge

---

## 11.4 TLS & Certificate Lifecycle

- **mTLS Everywhere**
    - All service-to-service communication uses mutual TLS with short-lived certs.
    - SPIFFE/SPIRE for automated X.509 issuance and rotation.
- **Certificate Management**
    - Root & intermediate CAs in HSM (CloudHSM)
    - CSR automation via ACME-DNS validation
    - Cert validity: 7 days max; automated rotate & revoke pipelines
- **Cryptographic Standards**
    - TLS 1.3 only, ciphers: TLS_AES_256_GCM_SHA384, CHACHA20_POLY1305_SHA256
    - Enforce forward secrecy, AEAD for all channels
    - HSTS + Preload, HPKP disabled in favor of mTLS

---

## 11.5 Key Management & HSM Integration

- **Hardware Security Modules**
    - AWS/GCP CloudHSM clusters in multi-AZ for high availability
    - Master keys never leave HSM; sign and decrypt operations via API
- **Secret Zero-Trust Workflow**
    1. **Bootstrap**: Vault Agent with AppRole pulls short-lived token
    2. **Fetch**: Request application secrets (node keys, DB creds) dynamically
    3. **Lease**: Secrets TTL ≤ 1 hour; auto-renew via Vault
    4. **Revoke**: On pod/container termination, revoke leases immediately
- **Auditing & Compliance**
    - All HSM API calls logged to secure SIEM in real-time
    - Vault audit logging shipped to central observability (Elastic/Datadog)

---

## 11.6 Continuous Security & Compliance

- **Runtime Threat Detection**
    - eBPF network visibility (Tracee) plus AI-driven anomaly detection
    - Alerts on unusual RPC patterns, chain reorg spikes
- **Configuration Compliance**
